WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.200
A.M.C. has put out more than its fair share
of hit television shows in the past several

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.666
years, but the undisputed cornerstone of the
network remains "The Walking Dead."

00:00:09.666 --> 00:00:15.480
Debuting on October 31, 2010, the program
offered a dramatic new spin on the zombie

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:20.340
genre by putting the focus on the human survivors
and their lives with one another and using

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:25.070
the reanimated masses - which aren't even
called "zombies" in the show - as a backdrop.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:29.380
This approach made the series a pop culture
phenomenon in no time and propelled it for

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.424
over a decade.

00:00:30.424 --> 00:00:35.920
While "The Walking Dead" is immensely popular,
it isn't exactly a show that's accessible to everyone.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.980
The collapse of modern society and the rise
of flesh-hungry corpses known as "walkers"

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.510
are enough to turn off viewers who are sensitive
to such content.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:50.510
Factor in the excessive blood, gore, and general
violence that constantly follow the characters,

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:54.662
elaborate special effects that make death
scenes look far too real, and the series'

00:00:54.662 --> 00:00:59.350
use of well-time jump scares, and you've got
a recipe for a show that is just too much

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:00.350
for some people.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:04.939
For the majority of "Walking Dead" viewers,
this content comes with the territory, and

00:01:04.939 --> 00:01:06.340
there are no complaints to be had.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:11.340
However, there are a few odd scenes that unsettled
even the most committed fans - and many have

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.950
confessed that a few "Walking Dead" moments
went way too far.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:21.096
We here at Looper were curious about the "Walking
Dead" fandom's picks for its most stomach-churning scenes.

00:01:21.096 --> 00:01:27.240
We polled viewers and according to our results,
almost 28% of respondents agreed that Negan

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:32.979
Smith brutally killing Glenn Rhee and Abraham
Ford was the hardest moment to handle.

00:01:32.979 --> 00:01:37.819
For those who don't recall, in the Season
7 premiere, ominously and aptly entitled "The

00:01:37.819 --> 00:01:43.689
Day Will Come When You Won't Be," Negan taunts
Rick Grimes and his group of fellow survivors,

00:01:43.689 --> 00:01:47.380
who he has ordered to kneel on the ground
and declare their loyalty to him.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:52.959
He chooses Abraham to make an example of,
using his barbed-wire-covered bat Lucille

00:01:52.959 --> 00:01:54.532
to bludgeon him in the head.

00:01:54.532 --> 00:01:59.959
When Daryl Dixon attempts to take a stand
and attack Negan, the bat wielding maniac

00:01:59.959 --> 00:02:01.528
has a simple response.

00:02:01.528 --> 00:02:04.915
"That, oh my.

00:02:06.177 --> 00:02:09.405
That is a no-no."

00:02:09.549 --> 00:02:12.263
Then, of course, things go from bad to worse.

00:02:12.263 --> 00:02:18.483
Negan decides that the group needs to be further
punished, and he selects Glenn as his next victim.

00:02:18.483 --> 00:02:22.224
He kills him without mercy, in the same way
that he did to Abraham.

00:02:22.224 --> 00:02:27.410
The brutal deaths of Glenn and Abraham have
been remembered in infamy, and even one of

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:31.518
the "Walking Dead" stars involved in the scene
thought it went too far.

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:36.670
During an appearance on the "Talk Dead to
Me" podcast, Abraham actor Michael Cudlitz

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.100
revealed his true feelings.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.560
"I always think it was a bridge too far, personally.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:42.930
I thought it was too much.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:47.331
Either one of us should have lived a little
bit longer, because people were very affected by it."

00:02:47.331 --> 00:02:52.239
Cudlitz added that he knows more gruesome
deaths happened in "The Walking Dead," but

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:56.760
Glenn and Abraham's struck viewers because
they truly cared about the characters.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:02.085
"There were a lot of other killings and murders
and lives lost on the show that were a lot more brutal.

00:03:02.085 --> 00:03:06.790
[But] the fact that I think you loved Abraham
and Glenn so much as an audience, that's what

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:07.959
makes it more brutal."

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:13.510
Unsurprisingly, for a show as gory as "The
Walking Dead," Negan's bloody executions weren't

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:17.360
totally unopposed in our poll about which
scenes went too far.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:21.322
The Season 3 episode "Killer Within" also
ranks high.

00:03:21.322 --> 00:03:26.900
It deals with the death of Rick's wife Lori,
who had to undergo an emergency C-section,

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.819
courtesy of Maggie Greene, to save her baby.

00:03:29.819 --> 00:03:34.840
That gut-wrenching scene culminates with Lori
and Rick's son Carl killing his mom before

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:36.340
she returns as a walker.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:39.815
From there, the picks don't get any less heartbreaking.

00:03:39.815 --> 00:03:45.049
The runners-up include Rick killing Sophie
in her walker form in front of her mom, along

00:03:45.049 --> 00:03:48.290
with Carol shooting the severely disturbed
Lizzie.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:53.678
And finally, Noah's demise at the hands of
a zombie horde rounds out the list.

00:03:53.678 --> 00:03:58.999
With more than 150 episodes to look back on,
this is surely just the tip of the iceberg

00:03:58.999 --> 00:04:03.279
when it comes to the show testing the limits
of cable television guidelines.

00:04:03.279 --> 00:04:08.819
Now that its historic run will wrap up in
2022, one has to wonder if "The Walking Dead"

00:04:08.819 --> 00:04:14.644
will try to push the envelope one more time
or have mercy on its fans and give us a hopeful ending.

00:04:14.644 --> 00:04:19.768
Either way, it's going to be tough to say
goodbye to the show and all its surviving characters.

00:04:19.999 --> 00:04:21.230
"It's an emotional moment.

00:04:21.878 --> 00:04:22.706
I get it."

